# Integrity Policy Enforcement: the kernel executes code only from the
# initramfs and from the dm-verity root of the image it was built for.
# Opt in with `--kernel-config-fragment kernel/ipe.config`, or copy these
# lines into your own fragment. Only for images that bake their workload
# into the root: nothing written at runtime executes (cloud-init runcmd
# included), and anonymous executable memory (JITs) is denied, so container
# hosts and JIT runtimes cannot use it. The policy is kernel/ipe-boot-policy,
# sealed to the image's root hash by `confos build` (src/kernel/ipe.rs).
# See docs/THREAT_MODEL.md.
CONFIG_SECURITYFS=y
CONFIG_SECURITY_IPE=y
CONFIG_IPE_BOOT_POLICY="security/ipe/confos-boot-policy"
# CONFIG_SECURITY_IPE_KUNIT_TEST is not set
